# figures/ and tables/ — what each file shows and where it comes from

Venue: NeurIPS 2026 (5.5 in text width, figure text ≥ 7 pt at print size, full-width figures ≤ 2.3 in high, vector PDF, TrueType fonts embedded). Figures are drawn at their printed size: include with `width=\linewidth` (`fig1.pdf` carries the 2.7 in protocol schematic as its left panel).
Rebuild: `figures/src/build.sh <paper-repo>/code/results` (from the repo root; writes `figures/*.pdf`, `tables/tab1.tex`, `tables/tab2.tex`). Each script prints the data it used (pool, truth, worlds, draws, interval kind). Result files and their columns: `DATA_CONTRACT.md` and experiment-repo's `code/results/README.md` (the authority on what each result is).

Type: every glyph prints at ≥ 7 pt at the placed width (checked with PyMuPDF on the built PDFs; mathtext indices are kept at label size, `figstyle.apply`). Fonts are embedded TrueType (type 42). Colours are Okabe–Ito/blue ramps and every distinction also differs in marker or line style (greyscale-safe). Tables need the packages `booktabs`, `array`.

## Status (result files of paper-repo `dev` at 45e05e9)
Intervals on `gap` (Figs 1, 2a, 2c) and on the C4 rates (Fig 3b, 3c real) are the corrected `total_ci` ones (pool-bootstrap spread with draw noise accounted for, plus the Monte-Carlo error of the point; e.g. gap at n = 30, exhaustive: 0.108–0.124); point estimates are unchanged. Real-arm files are in: Figs 1–6 and Tabs 1–2 are drawn from them. Tab 3 (C8) is drawn from `real_tool` and `real_tool_draws`; the compute row of Tab 1 waits for a compute column in `matrix_facts`. Intervals: real-arm panels are `pool-bootstrap` (R = 40 resampled pools, spread placed on the point estimate, 95%; coarse; they describe this 1,500-item pool, not another benchmark), synthetic panels `world-spread-t` (t-interval over simulated worlds); each caption must say which. Real protocol cells are scored as a pair (anti-conservative: truth = accuracy on the pool items outside U; conservative: truth plus 1.645 SE of that accuracy): Figs 4 and 5 draw the first with its interval and the second as a tick, Tab 2 carries only the first.

